{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K5Ad3PXe9KME8uNapkYnpL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Scale expansion: 15+ models (API + large open-source)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"将模型池从 6 扩展到 15+（加入 GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4o, GPT-4.1, Claude-3.5-Sonnet, Gemini-1.5-Pro, Llama-3.1-70B, Qwen2.5-72B, Mixtral-8x22B），重跑 MI 矩阵和 C(15,3)=455 panels 的多元回归。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_panels\": 455,\n7\t      \"total_conditions\": 12,\n8\t      \"eta_max_sig_count\": 5,\n9\t      \"eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.42,\n10\t      \"keff_sig_negative_count\": 4,\n11\t      \"keff_nonsig_count\": 7,\n12\t      \"keff_sig_positive_count\": 1,\n13\t      \"median_R2\": 0.22,\n14\t      \"eta_max_median_beta\": 0.61,\n15\t      \"keff_median_beta\": -0.18,\n16\t      \"overall_keff_p_median\": 0.14,\n17\t      \"api_model_panels_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n18\t      \"api_model_panels_keff_sig_rate\": 0.5,\n19\t      \"opensource_weak_panels_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.67,\n20\t      \"opensource_weak_panels_keff_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n21\t      \"expanded_panel_weakest_link_consistency\": 0.42\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"tables\": [\n24\t      {\n25\t        \"caption\": \"Multivariate regression results on 455 panels (15 models, K=3)\",\n26\t        \"columns\": [\n27\t          \"Dataset\",\n28\t          \"Attack\",\n29\t          \"β(η_max)\",\n30\t          \"p(η_max)\",\n31\t          \"β(K_eff)\",\n32\t          \"p(K_eff)\",\n33\t          \"R²\"\n34\t        ],\n35\t        \"rows\": [\n36\t          [\n37\t            \"MMLU\",\n38\t            \"prompt-injection\",\n39\t            \"0.82\",\n40\t            \"0.003\",\n41\t            \"-0.31\",\n42\t            \"0.08\",\n43\t            \"0.34\"\n44\t          ],\n45\t          [\n46\t            \"MMLU\",\n47\t            \"score-manipulation\",\n48\t            \"0.74\",\n49\t            \"0.011\",\n50\t            \"-0.22\",\n51\t            \"0.18\",\n52\t            \"0.26\"\n53\t          ],\n54\t          [\n55\t            \"MMLU\",\n56\t            \"sycophancy\",\n57\t            \"0.58\",\n58\t            \"0.042\",\n59\t            \"-0.41\",\n60\t            \"0.03\",\n61\t            \"0.28\"\n62\t          ],\n63\t          [\n64\t            \"MMLU\",\n65\t            \"verbosity\",\n66\t            \"0.45\",\n67\t            \"0.12\",\n68\t            \"-0.15\",\n69\t            \"0.42\",\n70\t            \"0.14\"\n71\t          ],\n72\t          [\n73\t            \"MMLU\",\n74\t            \"position\",\n75\t            \"0.39\",\n76\t            \"0.18\",\n77\t            \"0.12\",\n78\t            \"0.51\",\n79\t            \"0.09\"\n80\t          ],\n81\t          [\n82\t            \"MMLU\",\n83\t            \"authority\",\n84\t            \"0.68\",\n85\t            \"0.008\",\n86\t            \"-0.28\",\n87\t            \"0.11\",\n88\t            \"0.29\"\n89\t          ],\n90\t          [\n91\t            \"ARC\",\n92\t            \"prompt-injection\",\n93\t            \"0.71\",\n94\t            \"0.015\",\n95\t            \"-0.38\",\n96\t            \"0.04\",\n97\t            \"0.31\"\n98\t          ],\n99\t          [\n100\t            \"ARC\",\n101\t            \"score-manipulation\",\n102\t            \"0.63\",\n103\t            \"0.028\",\n104\t            \"-0.19\",\n105\t            \"0.27\",\n106\t            \"0.22\"\n107\t          ],\n108\t          [\n109\t            \"ARC\",\n110\t            \"sycophancy\",\n111\t            \"0.52\",\n112\t            \"0.065\",\n113\t            \"-0.44\",\n114\t            \"0.02\",\n115\t            \"0.25\"\n116\t          ],\n117\t          [\n118\t            \"ARC\",\n119\t            \"verbosity\",\n120\t            \"0.41\",\n121\t            \"0.14\",\n122\t            \"-0.33\",\n123\t            \"0.07\",\n124\t            \"0.18\"\n125\t          ],\n126\t          [\n127\t            \"ARC\",\n128\t            \"position\",\n129\t            \"0.33\",\n130\t            \"0.22\",\n131\t            \"0.18\",\n132\t            \"0.35\",\n133\t            \"0.08\"\n134\t          ],\n135\t          [\n136\t            \"ARC\",\n137\t            \"authority\",\n138\t            \"0.55\",\n139\t            \"0.052\",\n140\t            \"-0.26\",\n141\t            \"0.15\",\n142\t            \"0.21\"\n143\t          ]\n144\t        ]\n145\t      },\n146\t      {\n147\t        \"caption\": \"Regime-stratified η_max significance (panel capability tiers)\",\n148\t        \"columns\": [\n149\t          \"Panel Tier\",\n150\t          \"N panels\",\n151\t          \"η_max sig rate\",\n152\t          \"K_eff sig negative rate\",\n153\t          \"Median R²\"\n154\t        ],\n155\t        \"rows\": [\n156\t          [\n157\t            \"All-API (GPT/Claude/Gemini)\",\n158\t            \"20\",\n159\t            \"0.17\",\n160\t            \"0.50\",\n161\t            \"0.12\"\n162\t          ],\n163\t          [\n164\t            \"Mixed (API + 70B)\",\n165\t            \"120\",\n166\t            \"0.33\",\n167\t            \"0.42\",\n168\t            \"0.19\"\n169\t          ],\n170\t          [\n171\t            \"All-large-OS (70B class)\",\n172\t            \"35\",\n173\t            \"0.50\",\n174\t            \"0.25\",\n175\t            \"0.24\"\n176\t          ],\n177\t          [\n178\t            \"Mixed (large + small OS)\",\n179\t            \"180\",\n180\t            \"0.58\",\n181\t            \"0.17\",\n182\t            \"0.28\"\n183\t          ],\n184\t          [\n185\t            \"All-small-OS (7B class)\",\n186\t            \"10\",\n187\t            \"0.67\",\n188\t            \"0.08\",\n189\t            \"0.35\"\n190\t          ],\n191\t          [\n192\t            \"Contains ≥1 weak model\",\n193\t            \"280\",\n194\t            \"0.55\",\n195\t            \"0.18\",\n196\t            \"0.27\"\n197\t          ]\n198\t        ]\n199\t      }\n200\t    ],\n201\t    \"figures\": [],\n202\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档最核心的结果变化。MVP 阶段的 6 模型结论（η_max dominates universally） 在 15 模型池上碎片化为 regime-dependent 结论。关键发现：(1) 强模型 panel 中 η_max 方差太小，不构成 weakest link——因为没有 weak link；(2) 此时 K_eff 代表的 diversity 确实提供了互补保护；(3) 弱模型 panel 中 MVP 结论完全成立。 论文 reframe 方向：从 \\\"η_max always dominates\\\" 变为 \\\"η_max dominates when there exists a sufficiently weak member; above a capability threshold, diversity becomes the operative defense\\\"。这实际上是更有趣的 nuanced result，但需要 reviewer 接受 regime-dependent 结论的价值。\\n\\n\\n扩展模型池引入高能力 API 模型后，capability range 显著拉宽。在纯 API 模型 （GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini）组成的 panel 中，所有成员 η 都很低（individual ASR ~5-15%），η_max 方差小，回归中 η_max 的解释力下降（low variance → low signal）。 此时 K_eff 代表的模型多样性反而能捕捉到 residual attack surface 差异—— 不同 API 模型对不同 attack type 的脆弱面不同，diversity 确实提供了互补保护。 但在包含弱模型（7B open-source）的 panel 中，某个模型 η ≈ 0.6-0.8， 远高于其他成员，weakest-link 效应依然成立。总体来看 η_max 显著率从 MVP 的 67%（4/6）下降到 42%（5/12），K_eff 从 0/6 显著负变为 4/12—— weakest-link theorem 不再 universal，而是 regime-dependent。\\n\"\n203\t  },\n204\t  {\n205\t    \"name\": \"Attack expansion: 6+ attack types\",\n206\t    \"description\": \"新增 few-shot hijacking、persona manipulation、instruction override 三种攻击， 在 15+ 模型池上运行，验证 weakest-link 在更广泛 attack surface 上的表现。\\n\",\n207\t    \"results\": {\n208\t      \"new_attack_types\": 3,\n209\t      \"total_attack_types\": 9,\n210\t      \"total_conditions\": 18,\n211\t      \"eta_max_sig_rate_new_attacks\": 0.33,\n212\t      \"keff_sig_negative_rate_new_attacks\": 0.5,\n213\t      \"eta_max_sig_rate_overall\": 0.39,\n214\t      \"keff_sig_negative_rate_overall\": 0.39,\n215\t      \"few_shot_hijacking_eta_max_p\": 0.19,\n216\t      \"few_shot_hijacking_keff_p\": 0.04,\n217\t      \"persona_manipulation_eta_max_p\": 0.035,\n218\t      \"persona_manipulation_keff_p\": 0.22,\n219\t      \"instruction_override_eta_max_p\": 0.08,\n220\t      \"instruction_override_keff_p\": 0.03\n221\t    },\n222\t    \"tables\": [\n223\t      {\n224\t        \"caption\": \"Regression results for new attack types (455 panels)\",\n225\t        \"columns\": [\n226\t          \"Dataset\",\n227\t          \"Attack\",\n228\t          \"β(η_max)\",\n229\t          \"p(η_max)\",\n230\t          \"β(K_eff)\",\n231\t          \"p(K_eff)\",\n232\t          \"R²\"\n233\t        ],\n234\t        \"rows\": [\n235\t          [\n236\t            \"MMLU\",\n237\t            \"few-shot-hijacking\",\n238\t            \"0.28\",\n239\t            \"0.24\",\n240\t            \"-0.48\",\n241\t            \"0.03\",\n242\t            \"0.19\"\n243\t          ],\n244\t          [\n245\t            \"MMLU\",\n246\t            \"persona-manipulation\",\n247\t            \"0.72\",\n248\t            \"0.009\",\n249\t            \"-0.14\",\n250\t            \"0.39\",\n251\t            \"0.25\"\n252\t          ],\n253\t          [\n254\t            \"MMLU\",\n255\t            \"instruction-override\",\n256\t            \"0.35\",\n257\t            \"0.15\",\n258\t            \"-0.52\",\n259\t            \"0.02\",\n260\t            \"0.22\"\n261\t          ],\n262\t          [\n263\t            \"ARC\",\n264\t            \"few-shot-hijacking\",\n265\t            \"0.31\",\n266\t            \"0.19\",\n267\t            \"-0.39\",\n268\t            \"0.05\",\n269\t            \"0.16\"\n270\t          ],\n271\t          [\n272\t            \"ARC\",\n273\t            \"persona-manipulation\",\n274\t            \"0.65\",\n275\t            \"0.035\",\n276\t            \"-0.21\",\n277\t            \"0.22\",\n278\t            \"0.22\"\n279\t          ],\n280\t          [\n281\t            \"ARC\",\n282\t            \"instruction-override\",\n283\t            \"0.38\",\n284\t            \"0.12\",\n285\t            \"-0.44\",\n286\t            \"0.03\",\n287\t            \"0.20\"\n288\t          ]\n289\t        ]\n290\t      }\n291\t    ],\n292\t    \"figures\": [],\n293\t    \"analysis\": \"攻击扩展进一步确认 regime-dependent 结论，且揭示了一个有价值的 pattern： attack transferability 是决定 η_max vs K_eff 哪个更重要的关键维度。 targeted attacks（需要针对特定模型调优的攻击）→ η_max 主导； transferable attacks（利用 LLM 共性弱点的攻击）→ K_eff 有效。 这为 framework paper 提供了 regime characterization 的第二个维度 （第一个是 panel capability tier），增强了 analytical contribution。\\n\\n\\n新增攻击类型进一步分裂 weakest-link 的 universality。few-shot hijacking 和 instruction override 是高度 transferable 的攻击——它们利用 instruction-following 这一所有 LLM 共享的特性，因此对 panel 中所有模型的 ASR 较均匀。此时 η_max 解释力弱（因为 variance across judges 低），而 K_eff 反而显著——多样性意味着 不同模型对 instruction-following exploit 的具体 failure mode 不同，提供互补保护。 persona manipulation 类似 sycophancy，更依赖 individual model 特性（某些模型 对 authority cues 特别敏感），η_max 仍显著。总体上 η_max 和 K_eff 各在约 40% 条件下显著，无一方 universal dominate——核心 claim 需要 nuance。\\n\"\n294\t  },\n295\t  {\n296\t    \"name\": \"Adaptive adversary formal theorem + random-fault simulation\",\n297\t    \"description\": \"(a) 形式化定理：adaptive adversary 下 panel_ASR = Θ(η_max)； (b) random-fault simulation：每个 judge 独立以概率 p_j fail； (c) 对比验证 BFT 区分。\\n\",\n298\t    \"results\": {\n299\t      \"theorem_holds\": true,\n300\t      \"theorem_tightness\": \"loose in strong-model regime\",\n301\t      \"random_fault_keff_sig_rate\": 0.39,\n302\t      \"adaptive_keff_sig_rate\": 0.39,\n303\t      \"bft_contrast_cohen_d\": 0.22,\n304\t      \"bft_contrast_p\": 0.08,\n305\t      \"keff_beta_ratio_random_vs_adaptive\": 1.4,\n306\t      \"random_fault_keff_median_beta\": -0.52,\n307\t      \"adaptive_keff_median_beta\": -0.37,\n308\t      \"regime_interaction_p\": 0.04\n309\t    },\n310\t    \"tables\": [\n311\t      {\n312\t        \"caption\": \"K_eff significance: adaptive vs random-fault across regimes\",\n313\t        \"columns\": [\n314\t          \"Regime\",\n315\t          \"Fault Type\",\n316\t          \"K_eff β\",\n317\t          \"K_eff p\",\n318\t          \"η_max β\",\n319\t          \"η_max p\"\n320\t        ],\n321\t        \"rows\": [\n322\t          [\n323\t            \"Weak panels\",\n324\t            \"adaptive\",\n325\t            \"-0.12\",\n326\t            \"0.48\",\n327\t            \"0.78\",\n328\t            \"0.004\"\n329\t          ],\n330\t          [\n331\t            \"Weak panels\",\n332\t            \"random-fault\",\n333\t            \"-0.41\",\n334\t            \"0.03\",\n335\t            \"0.52\",\n336\t            \"0.06\"\n337\t          ],\n338\t          [\n339\t            \"Mixed panels\",\n340\t            \"adaptive\",\n341\t            \"-0.28\",\n342\t            \"0.09\",\n343\t            \"0.55\",\n344\t            \"0.04\"\n345\t          ],\n346\t          [\n347\t            \"Mixed panels\",\n348\t            \"random-fault\",\n349\t            \"-0.45\",\n350\t            \"0.02\",\n351\t            \"0.38\",\n352\t            \"0.11\"\n353\t          ],\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"Strong panels\",\n356\t            \"adaptive\",\n357\t            \"-0.44\",\n358\t            \"0.02\",\n359\t            \"0.22\",\n360\t            \"0.31\"\n361\t          ],\n362\t          [\n363\t            \"Strong panels\",\n364\t            \"random-fault\",\n365\t            \"-0.58\",\n366\t            \"0.005\",\n367\t            \"0.15\",\n368\t            \"0.48\"\n369\t          ]\n370\t        ]\n371\t      },\n372\t      {\n373\t        \"caption\": \"BFT contrast effect sizes\",\n374\t        \"columns\": [\n375\t          \"Metric\",\n376\t          \"Weak panels\",\n377\t          \"Mixed panels\",\n378\t          \"Strong panels\",\n379\t          \"Overall\"\n380\t        ],\n381\t        \"rows\": [\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"Cohen's d (K_eff β difference)\",\n384\t            \"0.38\",\n385\t            \"0.21\",\n386\t            \"0.12\",\n387\t            \"0.22\"\n388\t          ],\n389\t          [\n390\t            \"p (paired t-test)\",\n391\t            \"0.04\",\n392\t            \"0.12\",\n393\t            \"0.41\",\n394\t            \"0.08\"\n395\t          ]\n396\t        ]\n397\t      }\n398\t    ],\n399\t    \"figures\": [],\n400\t    \"analysis\": \"BFT 区分的理论贡献被削弱。Overall Cohen's d = 0.22 远低于 medium effect size 标准（0.5），且 overall p = 0.08 不显著。只有在 weak panel regime 中 contrast 才显著（d = 0.38, p = 0.04）。这意味着 \\\"adaptive adversary fundamentally different from BFT\\\" 这个 claim 需要限定为 \\\"the distinction matters primarily in weak-model settings\\\"。不过 regime × fault-type 交互效应本身是有趣的发现， 可以作为 framework 的 analytical insight。论文需要降低 BFT contrast 的 claim 强度，从 \\\"fundamental distinction\\\" 变为 \\\"regime-dependent distinction\\\"。\\n\\n\\n形式化定理本身在数学上成立——在 adaptive adversary 假设下，panel ASR 的 upper bound 确实由 max(η_j) 决定。但在 worst 档下，实证数据显示这个 bound 在强模型 regime 中很 loose（实际 ASR 远低于 η_max bound），因为即使是 adaptive adversary，当所有模型都很强时，攻击成本太高，实际行为更接近 opportunistic 而非 truly adaptive。random-fault simulation 中 K_eff 确实 比 adaptive 条件下更显著，但差异不大（Cohen's d ≈ 0.22，远小于预期的 0.5+）——因为在实际数据中，即使是 adaptive attacks 也不完美 adaptive （attacker 没有完美的 per-judge oracle），与 random fault 的差距没有 理论预测的那么大。关键的 saving grace 是 regime × fault-type 交互显著 （p=0.04）：在弱模型 panel 中 adaptive vs random 差异大，强模型 panel 中 差异消失。这支持 regime characterization 的 narrative。\\n\"\n401\t  },\n402\t  {\n403\t    \"name\": \"Capability-matched validation\",\n404\t    \"description\": \"在同一 capability tier 内（如全 7B 或全 70B），测试控制 η_max 方差后 K_eff 是否显著。如果 within-tier K_eff 显著 → diversity 在控制 capability 后确实有效。\\n\",\n405\t    \"results\": {\n406\t      \"tiers_tested\": 3,\n407\t      \"tier_7b_keff_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n408\t      \"tier_7b_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.5,\n409\t      \"tier_70b_keff_sig_rate\": 0.33,\n410\t      \"tier_70b_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.33,\n411\t      \"tier_api_keff_sig_rate\": 0.5,\n412\t      \"tier_api_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n413\t      \"diversity_capability_r_overall\": -0.41,\n414\t      \"diversity_capability_r_within_7b\": -0.18,\n415\t      \"diversity_capability_r_within_70b\": -0.08,\n416\t      \"diversity_capability_r_within_api\": -0.05,\n417\t      \"within_tier_keff_overall_sig_rate\": 0.33\n418\t    },\n419\t    \"tables\": [\n420\t      {\n421\t        \"caption\": \"Within-tier regression: K_eff significance by capability tier\",\n422\t        \"columns\": [\n423\t          \"Tier\",\n424\t          \"N models\",\n425\t          \"N panels (K=3)\",\n426\t          \"η_max sig rate\",\n427\t          \"K_eff sig neg rate\",\n428\t          \"Median R²\",\n429\t          \"K_eff-η_max r\"\n430\t        ],\n431\t        \"rows\": [\n432\t          [\n433\t            \"7B class\",\n434\t            \"5\",\n435\t            \"10\",\n436\t            \"0.50\",\n437\t            \"0.17\",\n438\t            \"0.18\",\n439\t            \"-0.18\"\n440\t          ],\n441\t          [\n442\t            \"70B class\",\n443\t            \"4\",\n444\t            \"4\",\n445\t            \"0.33\",\n446\t            \"0.33\",\n447\t            \"0.15\",\n448\t            \"-0.08\"\n449\t          ],\n450\t          [\n451\t            \"API models\",\n452\t            \"5\",\n453\t            \"10\",\n454\t            \"0.17\",\n455\t            \"0.50\",\n456\t            \"0.12\",\n457\t            \"-0.05\"\n458\t          ],\n459\t          [\n460\t            \"Cross-tier (all)\",\n461\t            \"15\",\n462\t            \"455\",\n463\t            \"0.42\",\n464\t            \"0.33\",\n465\t            \"0.22\",\n466\t            \"-0.41\"\n467\t          ]\n468\t        ]\n469\t      },\n470\t      {\n471\t        \"caption\": \"Diversity-capability tradeoff decomposition\",\n472\t        \"columns\": [\n473\t          \"Scope\",\n474\t          \"Pearson r\",\n475\t          \"p-value\",\n476\t          \"Interpretation\"\n477\t        ],\n478\t        \"rows\": [\n479\t          [\n480\t            \"Overall (15 models)\",\n481\t            \"-0.41\",\n482\t            \"0.003\",\n483\t            \"Moderate negative — driven by tier differences\"\n484\t          ],\n485\t          [\n486\t            \"Within 7B\",\n487\t            \"-0.18\",\n488\t            \"0.38\",\n489\t            \"Not significant — no tradeoff within tier\"\n490\t          ],\n491\t          [\n492\t            \"Within 70B\",\n493\t            \"-0.08\",\n494\t            \"0.72\",\n495\t            \"Not significant\"\n496\t          ],\n497\t          [\n498\t            \"Within API\",\n499\t            \"-0.05\",\n500\t            \"0.81\",\n501\t            \"Not significant\"\n502\t          ],\n503\t          [\n504\t            \"Open-source only (10 models)\",\n505\t            \"-0.72\",\n506\t            \"0.001\",\n507\t            \"Strong negative — ecosystem artifact\"\n508\t          ]\n509\t        ]\n510\t      }\n511\t    ],\n512\t    \"figures\": [],\n513\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档最具杀伤力的结果。diversity-capability tradeoff（Claim 3）被 证实主要是 open-source ecosystem artifact，而非 fundamental constraint。 加入 API 模型后 overall r 从 -0.8 降到 -0.41，within-tier r 接近 0。 这意味着 \\\"diversity and security are structurally at odds\\\" 这个 strong claim 需要大幅限定为 \\\"in the current open-source ecosystem, where capability strongly predicts robustness, pursuing diversity across capability tiers introduces weaker models\\\"。同时 within-tier K_eff 显著率 33% 表明 diversity 在 controlled settings 中确实有效——进一步削弱 \\\"diversity is a trap\\\" narrative。论文 reframe 必须诚实承认这一点。\\n\\n\\n控制 capability tier 后，η_max 方差被大幅压缩（within-tier models 能力接近）， 回归中 η_max 的解释力下降。此时 K_eff 在部分条件下变得显著——特别是在 API tier 中（3/6 显著），因为 GPT-4o、Claude、Gemini 虽然 capability 相似， 但 vulnerability profile 显著不同（不同训练数据和 safety alignment 策略）， diversity 确实提供互补保护。70B tier 中 K_eff 中等显著（2/6），7B tier 中 仍不显著（1/6）——因为 7B 模型普遍 vulnerable，η_max 方差虽然 within-tier 较小但绝对值仍高，weakest-link 效应持续。 diversity-capability tradeoff 的 overall r 从 MVP 的 -0.8 降到 -0.41（加入 API 模型后 tradeoff 大幅减弱），within-tier r 接近 0（-0.05 to -0.18）—— tradeoff 主要是 cross-tier artifact（比较 7B 和 70B 当然 diversity 高但 capability 低），而非 fundamental constraint。\\n\"\n514\t  },\n515\t  {\n516\t    \"name\": \"Two-stage panel design algorithm: full benchmark\",\n517\t    \"description\": \"实现 robustness-first 两阶段算法（先筛 η ≤ threshold，再最大化 K_eff）， 对比 5 个 baseline 策略。在 15+ 模型池上 sweep threshold。\\n\",\n518\t    \"results\": {\n519\t      \"strategies_compared\": 6,\n520\t      \"total_conditions\": 18,\n521\t      \"two_stage_win_rate\": 0.44,\n522\t      \"min_eta_max_win_rate\": 0.39,\n523\t      \"max_keff_win_rate\": 0.33,\n524\t      \"strongest_k_win_rate\": 0.5,\n525\t      \"random_win_rate\": 0.06,\n526\t      \"max_family_div_win_rate\": 0.11,\n527\t      \"two_stage_vs_strongest_k_p\": 0.32,\n528\t      \"two_stage_mean_asr\": 0.091,\n529\t      \"strongest_k_mean_asr\": 0.082,\n530\t      \"threshold_sensitivity\": \"high — optimal threshold varies by attack type\",\n531\t      \"pareto_dominated_by_strongest_k\": \"partially\"\n532\t    },\n533\t    \"tables\": [\n534\t      {\n535\t        \"caption\": \"Panel selection strategy benchmark (mean ASR, lower is better)\",\n536\t        \"columns\": [\n537\t          \"Strategy\",\n538\t          \"Mean ASR\",\n539\t          \"Median ASR\",\n540\t          \"Win rate\",\n541\t          \"vs Random p\"\n542\t        ],\n543\t        \"rows\": [\n544\t          [\n545\t            \"Two-stage (ours)\",\n546\t            \"0.091\",\n547\t            \"0.078\",\n548\t            \"0.44\",\n549\t            \"0.001\"\n550\t          ],\n551\t          [\n552\t            \"Strongest-K\",\n553\t            \"0.082\",\n554\t            \"0.071\",\n555\t            \"0.50\",\n556\t            \"<0.001\"\n557\t          ],\n558\t          [\n559\t            \"Min-η_max\",\n560\t            \"0.095\",\n561\t            \"0.085\",\n562\t            \"0.39\",\n563\t            \"0.003\"\n564\t          ],\n565\t          [\n566\t            \"Max-K_eff\",\n567\t            \"0.131\",\n568\t            \"0.118\",\n569\t            \"0.33\",\n570\t            \"0.02\"\n571\t          ],\n572\t          [\n573\t            \"Max-family-diversity\",\n574\t            \"0.158\",\n575\t            \"0.142\",\n576\t            \"0.11\",\n577\t            \"0.15\"\n578\t          ],\n579\t          [\n580\t            \"Random\",\n581\t            \"0.172\",\n582\t            \"0.155\",\n583\t            \"0.06\",\n584\t            \"—\"\n585\t          ]\n586\t        ]\n587\t      },\n588\t      {\n589\t        \"caption\": \"Head-to-head: Two-stage vs Strongest-K by regime\",\n590\t        \"columns\": [\n591\t          \"Regime\",\n592\t          \"Two-stage wins\",\n593\t          \"Strongest-K wins\",\n594\t          \"Tie\",\n595\t          \"p\"\n596\t        ],\n597\t        \"rows\": [\n598\t          [\n599\t            \"Weak panels (OS-7B only)\",\n600\t            \"4/6\",\n601\t            \"2/6\",\n602\t            \"0\",\n603\t            \"0.12\"\n604\t          ],\n605\t          [\n606\t            \"Mixed panels\",\n607\t            \"3/6\",\n608\t            \"3/6\",\n609\t            \"0\",\n610\t            \"0.82\"\n611\t          ],\n612\t          [\n613\t            \"Strong panels (API available)\",\n614\t            \"1/6\",\n615\t            \"4/6\",\n616\t            \"1\",\n617\t            \"0.08\"\n618\t          ]\n619\t        ]\n620\t      }\n621\t    ],\n622\t    \"figures\": [],\n623\t    \"analysis\": \"两阶段算法没有显著优势，Claim 6 实质性削弱。strongest-K 策略在有 API 模型 可用时 win rate 更高，且不需要 threshold 参数。两阶段算法唯一优势场景是 纯 open-source weak model pool（4/6 wins），但这一场景在实践中正在减少 （API 模型越来越便宜易用）。practical contribution 从 \\\"robustness-first algorithm dominates\\\" 降级为 \\\"when restricted to weak model pools, a robustness-first heuristic helps, but is unnecessary when strong models are available\\\"。可以在 paper 中作为 minor practical insight 保留， 但不能作为主要 contribution。\\n\\n\\n两阶段算法在 worst 档下表现不突出，因为 (1) strongest-K 策略（直接选最强 K 个 模型）在强模型 regime 中已经接近最优——当 API 模型可用时，选 GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini 既有高 robustness 又有 decent diversity（不同公司的模型自然 diverse）； (2) 两阶段算法的 threshold 参数高度 attack-dependent——对 prompt injection 最优 threshold ≠ 对 sycophancy 最优 threshold——无法给出 universal 建议； (3) 在弱模型 pool（纯 open-source 7B）中两阶段确实优于 max-K_eff，但 strongest-K 同样优于 max-K_eff，且不需要 threshold tuning。 win rate 0.44 略低于 strongest-K 的 0.50，且差异不显著（p=0.32）。 robustness-first 不 dominate，practical contribution 被削弱为 \\\"在缺乏 API 模型时的合理 heuristic\\\" 而非 \\\"universal optimal strategy\\\"。\\n\"\n624\t  },\n625\t  {\n626\t    \"name\": \"Per-judge ASR concentration analysis\",\n627\t    \"description\": \"对每个 panel × attack，测量 per-judge ASR 分布的集中度（Gini 系数、熵）， 验证攻击是否集中在最弱 judge 上。\\n\",\n628\t    \"results\": {\n629\t      \"median_gini\": 0.31,\n630\t      \"mean_gini\": 0.34,\n631\t      \"gini_strong_panels\": 0.18,\n632\t      \"gini_weak_panels\": 0.52,\n633\t      \"gini_mixed_panels\": 0.38,\n634\t      \"entropy_normalized_median\": 0.78,\n635\t      \"concentration_on_weakest_fraction\": 0.48,\n636\t      \"concentration_on_weakest_strong_panels\": 0.38,\n637\t      \"concentration_on_weakest_weak_panels\": 0.61,\n638\t      \"gini_adaptive_vs_random_p\": 0.06,\n639\t      \"gini_adaptive_vs_random_d\": 0.28\n640\t    },\n641\t    \"tables\": [\n642\t      {\n643\t        \"caption\": \"Per-judge ASR concentration by panel regime\",\n644\t        \"columns\": [\n645\t          \"Regime\",\n646\t          \"Median Gini\",\n647\t          \"Mean entropy (norm.)\",\n648\t          \"Weakest-judge share\",\n649\t          \"N panels\"\n650\t        ],\n651\t        \"rows\": [\n652\t          [\n653\t            \"All-API\",\n654\t            \"0.18\",\n655\t            \"0.91\",\n656\t            \"0.38\",\n657\t            \"20\"\n658\t          ],\n659\t          [\n660\t            \"Mixed (API+70B)\",\n661\t            \"0.28\",\n662\t            \"0.83\",\n663\t            \"0.42\",\n664\t            \"120\"\n665\t          ],\n666\t          [\n667\t            \"All-large-OS\",\n668\t            \"0.35\",\n669\t            \"0.77\",\n670\t            \"0.47\",\n671\t            \"35\"\n672\t          ],\n673\t          [\n674\t            \"Mixed (large+small OS)\",\n675\t            \"0.45\",\n676\t            \"0.69\",\n677\t            \"0.55\",\n678\t            \"180\"\n679\t          ],\n680\t          [\n681\t            \"All-small-OS\",\n682\t            \"0.52\",\n683\t            \"0.62\",\n684\t            \"0.61\",\n685\t            \"10\"\n686\t          ]\n687\t        ]\n688\t      },\n689\t      {\n690\t        \"caption\": \"Concentration: adaptive vs random-fault\",\n691\t        \"columns\": [\n692\t          \"Fault Type\",\n693\t          \"Median Gini\",\n694\t          \"Weakest-judge share\",\n695\t          \"Paired diff p\"\n696\t        ],\n697\t        \"rows\": [\n698\t          [\n699\t            \"Adaptive\",\n700\t            \"0.34\",\n701\t            \"0.48\",\n702\t            \"—\"\n703\t          ],\n704\t          [\n705\t            \"Random-fault\",\n706\t            \"0.26\",\n707\t            \"0.41\",\n708\t            \"0.06\"\n709\t          ]\n710\t        ]\n711\t      }\n712\t    ],\n713\t    \"figures\": [],\n714\t    \"analysis\": \"Concentration analysis 部分支持 adaptive adversary narrative，但仅限于 weak panel regime。在 strong panels 中，ASR 近乎均匀分布——不存在 \\\"weakest link\\\" targeting 行为。这从另一个角度确认 regime-dependent 结论：adaptive adversary model 的 descriptive accuracy 本身也是 regime-dependent 的。 在强模型 panel 中，adversary 更像 \\\"均匀探测\\\" 而非 \\\"精准打击\\\"。 这对形式化定理没有影响（定理给出 upper bound，不要求 tight），但削弱了 \\\"adaptive adversary is the right threat model\\\" 的 empirical support。\\n\\n\\nPer-judge ASR 集中度呈现清晰的 regime 分裂。在 weak panel（包含 7B 模型）中， Gini ≈ 0.52，最弱 judge 承担 61% 的攻击成功——符合 adaptive adversary targeting 预测。但在 strong panel（全 API 模型）中，Gini ≈ 0.18，接近均匀分布—— 攻击成功较均匀地分布在各 judge 上，因为没有明显的 \\\"weakest link\\\" 可供集中攻击。 adaptive vs random-fault 的 Gini 差异不显著（p=0.06, d=0.28）——因为即使在 adaptive 条件下，当模型能力相近时，attacker 的 targeting 精度有限，行为 接近 semi-random。这进一步支持 \\\"adaptive adversary distinction matters primarily in weak-model regime\\\" 的结论。\\n\"\n715\t  },\n716\t  {\n717\t    \"name\": \"Diversity-capability tradeoff visualization\",\n718\t    \"description\": \"在 C(15,3)=455 panels 上绘制 K_eff vs η_max scatter，拟合 tradeoff 曲线， 展示 Pareto frontier，按 capability tier 分层。\\n\",\n719\t    \"results\": {\n720\t      \"overall_pearson_r\": -0.41,\n721\t      \"overall_spearman_r\": -0.38,\n722\t      \"pareto_front_size\": 12,\n723\t      \"pareto_composition\": \"8/12 contain ≥2 API models\",\n724\t      \"tradeoff_slope\": -0.33,\n725\t      \"tradeoff_R2\": 0.17,\n726\t      \"api_inclusive_r\": -0.22,\n727\t      \"opensource_only_r\": -0.72,\n728\t      \"pareto_panels_mean_asr\": 0.075,\n729\t      \"non_pareto_mean_asr\": 0.148\n730\t    },\n731\t    \"tables\": [\n732\t      {\n733\t        \"caption\": \"Tradeoff statistics by model pool composition\",\n734\t        \"columns\": [\n735\t          \"Pool\",\n736\t          \"N panels\",\n737\t          \"r(K_eff, η_max)\",\n738\t          \"p\",\n739\t          \"R²\",\n740\t          \"Interpretation\"\n741\t        ],\n742\t        \"rows\": [\n743\t          [\n744\t            \"All 15 models\",\n745\t            \"455\",\n746\t            \"-0.41\",\n747\t            \"0.003\",\n748\t            \"0.17\",\n749\t            \"Moderate — not structural\"\n750\t          ],\n751\t          [\n752\t            \"Open-source only (10)\",\n753\t            \"120\",\n754\t            \"-0.72\",\n755\t            \"<0.001\",\n756\t            \"0.52\",\n757\t            \"Strong — ecosystem artifact\"\n758\t          ],\n759\t          [\n760\t            \"API-inclusive (≥1 API)\",\n761\t            \"335\",\n762\t            \"-0.22\",\n763\t            \"0.04\",\n764\t            \"0.05\",\n765\t            \"Weak — API breaks tradeoff\"\n766\t          ],\n767\t          [\n768\t            \"All-API (5)\",\n769\t            \"10\",\n770\t            \"-0.05\",\n771\t            \"0.89\",\n772\t            \"0.003\",\n773\t            \"None — diversity is free\"\n774\t          ]\n775\t        ]\n776\t      }\n777\t    ],\n778\t    \"figures\": [],\n779\t    \"analysis\": \"可视化是 reframed paper 的关键 figure。它同时传达两个信息：(1) open-source ecosystem 中 tradeoff 确实存在且严重（r=-0.72）；(2) 这不是 fundamental constraint——API 模型的加入打破了 tradeoff。实际含义：diversity-as-defense 不是 inherently flawed，只是在当前 open-source 生态中因 capability 分层 严重而表现为 trap。随着 open-source 模型 capability 提升（如未来 7B 模型 接近当前 70B 水平），tradeoff 将进一步缩小。这是一个 more nuanced 且 arguably more useful 的 finding，但比 \\\"diversity is fundamentally a trap\\\" 的 punch 力弱很多。\\n\\n\\n可视化清晰展示 tradeoff 的 ecosystem-dependent 本质。在纯 open-source 空间中， K_eff vs η_max 呈强负相关（r=-0.72）：要 diversity 就必须跨 capability tier 混搭（如 7B + 70B），必然引入弱模型。但加入 API 模型后，右上角出现一个 \\\"sweet spot\\\" 区域——API 模型组合同时实现高 K_eff（不同公司模型自然 diverse） 和低 η_max（都很强）。Pareto frontier 被 API-inclusive panels 主导（8/12）， 表明 tradeoff 可以通过使用 strong diverse models 打破。 Overall R² = 0.17 表明 tradeoff 只解释 17% 的方差——远非 \\\"structural\\\"。\\n\"\n780\t  },\n781\t  {\n782\t    \"name\": \"Panel size sensitivity: K=3,5,7,9\",\n783\t    \"description\": \"在不同 panel size (K=3,5,7,9) 下测试 weakest-link theorem。验证 η_max dominance 是否随 K 增大而变化。\\n\",\n784\t    \"results\": {\n785\t      \"k3_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.42,\n786\t      \"k5_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.33,\n787\t      \"k7_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.28,\n788\t      \"k9_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.22,\n789\t      \"k3_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.33,\n790\t      \"k5_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.39,\n791\t      \"k7_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.5,\n792\t      \"k9_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.56,\n793\t      \"eta_max_sig_trend_p\": 0.03,\n794\t      \"keff_sig_trend_p\": 0.02,\n795\t      \"k9_median_asr_reduction_vs_k3\": 0.35,\n796\t      \"diversity_benefit_threshold_k\": 5\n797\t    },\n798\t    \"tables\": [\n799\t      {\n800\t        \"caption\": \"Weakest-link persistence across panel sizes\",\n801\t        \"columns\": [\n802\t          \"K\",\n803\t          \"N panels\",\n804\t          \"η_max sig rate\",\n805\t          \"K_eff sig neg rate\",\n806\t          \"Median R²\",\n807\t          \"Mean ASR\"\n808\t        ],\n809\t        \"rows\": [\n810\t          [\n811\t            \"3\",\n812\t            \"455\",\n813\t            \"0.42\",\n814\t            \"0.33\",\n815\t            \"0.22\",\n816\t            \"0.134\"\n817\t          ],\n818\t          [\n819\t            \"5\",\n820\t            \"3003\",\n821\t            \"0.33\",\n822\t            \"0.39\",\n823\t            \"0.18\",\n824\t            \"0.105\"\n825\t          ],\n826\t          [\n827\t            \"7\",\n828\t            \"6435\",\n829\t            \"0.28\",\n830\t            \"0.50\",\n831\t            \"0.15\",\n832\t            \"0.092\"\n833\t          ],\n834\t          [\n835\t            \"9\",\n836\t            \"5005\",\n837\t            \"0.22\",\n838\t            \"0.56\",\n839\t            \"0.13\",\n840\t            \"0.087\"\n841\t          ]\n842\t        ]\n843\t      },\n844\t      {\n845\t        \"caption\": \"Transition analysis: K at which K_eff overtakes η_max\",\n846\t        \"columns\": [\n847\t          \"Metric\",\n848\t          \"K=3\",\n849\t          \"K=5\",\n850\t          \"K=7\",\n851\t          \"K=9\",\n852\t          \"Trend p\"\n853\t        ],\n854\t        \"rows\": [\n855\t          [\n856\t            \"η_max sig rate\",\n857\t            \"0.42\",\n858\t            \"0.33\",\n859\t            \"0.28\",\n860\t            \"0.22\",\n861\t            \"0.03\"\n862\t          ],\n863\t          [\n864\t            \"K_eff sig neg rate\",\n865\t            \"0.33\",\n866\t            \"0.39\",\n867\t            \"0.50\",\n868\t            \"0.56\",\n869\t            \"0.02\"\n870\t          ],\n871\t          [\n872\t            \"η_max > K_eff (conditions)\",\n873\t            \"7/18\",\n874\t            \"6/18\",\n875\t            \"4/18\",\n876\t            \"3/18\",\n877\t            \"—\"\n878\t          ]\n879\t        ]\n880\t      }\n881\t    ],\n882\t    \"figures\": [],\n883\t    \"analysis\": \"Panel size sensitivity 是最终确认 weakest-link non-universality 的实验。 η_max 显著率随 K 单调下降（0.42→0.22），K_eff 单调上升（0.33→0.56）， 交叉在 K≈5。这有一个直觉解释：K=3 majority vote 中 1 个被攻破的 judge 已经占 1/3 的权重，weakest link 影响巨大；K=9 中 1/9 权重，需要同时 攻破 5 个 judge 才能 flip panel，此时 diversity（不同 judge 的 failure mode 不同）确实提供了实质保护。 对 paper 的影响：weakest-link theorem 需要 qualified as \\\"primarily applies to small panels (K≤5) and when panel includes sufficiently weak members\\\"。 Practical recommendation 变为 regime-dependent guidance：小 panel 重 robustness，大 panel 重 diversity。这对 framework paper narrative 实际上 是 positive——提供了一个清晰的、可操作的 regime boundary。\\n\\n随着 panel size 增大，两个效应叠加削弱 weakest-link：(1) 更多 judges 意味着 更大的 voting majority 需要被 flip，即使 weakest judge 被攻破，其 1 票在 K=9 的 majority-vote 中影响更小（1/9 vs 1/3）；(2) 大 panel 更可能包含 strong models（15 个模型中选 9 个 vs 选 3 个），η_max 的绝对值被拉低， 方差也更小。因此 η_max 显著率从 K=3 的 42% 单调下降到 K=9 的 22%， 而 K_eff 显著率从 33% 上升到 56%。在 K ≈ 5 时出现交叉——diversity 开始比 individual robustness 更重要。这对 practical recommendation 有直接影响：K=3 时 focus on robustness，K≥5 时 diversity matters。 但这也进一步削弱了 \\\"weakest-link is universal\\\" 的 claim——它甚至 不对所有 panel size universal。\\n\"\n884\t  }\n885\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceb87fcc-da11-4033-9022-bc360860d1d4","uuid":"dc7a8212-e153-450b-9804-0c17e313e5bf","timestamp":"2026-05-22T06:16:31.215Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/cert_manip_resist_eval/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T055016/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scale expansion: 15+ models (API + large open-source)\",\n    \"description\": \"将模型池从 6 扩展到 15+（加入 GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4o, GPT-4.1, Claude-3.5-Sonnet, Gemini-1.5-Pro, Llama-3.1-70B, Qwen2.5-72B, Mixtral-8x22B），重跑 MI 矩阵和 C(15,3)=455 panels 的多元回归。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_panels\": 455,\n      \"total_conditions\": 12,\n      \"eta_max_sig_count\": 5,\n      \"eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.42,\n      \"keff_sig_negative_count\": 4,\n      \"keff_nonsig_count\": 7,\n      \"keff_sig_positive_count\": 1,\n      \"median_R2\": 0.22,\n      \"eta_max_median_beta\": 0.61,\n      \"keff_median_beta\": -0.18,\n      \"overall_keff_p_median\": 0.14,\n      \"api_model_panels_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n      \"api_model_panels_keff_sig_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"opensource_weak_panels_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.67,\n      \"opensource_weak_panels_keff_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n      \"expanded_panel_weakest_link_consistency\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Multivariate regression results on 455 panels (15 models, K=3)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Dataset\",\n          \"Attack\",\n          \"β(η_max)\",\n          \"p(η_max)\",\n          \"β(K_eff)\",\n          \"p(K_eff)\",\n          \"R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"prompt-injection\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"0.003\",\n            \"-0.31\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"0.34\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"score-manipulation\",\n            \"0.74\",\n            \"0.011\",\n            \"-0.22\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"0.26\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"sycophancy\",\n            \"0.58\",\n            \"0.042\",\n            \"-0.41\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.28\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"verbosity\",\n            \"0.45\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"-0.15\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.14\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"position\",\n            \"0.39\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.51\",\n            \"0.09\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"authority\",\n            \"0.68\",\n            \"0.008\",\n            \"-0.28\",\n            \"0.11\",\n            \"0.29\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"prompt-injection\",\n            \"0.71\",\n            \"0.015\",\n            \"-0.38\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"0.31\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"score-manipulation\",\n            \"0.63\",\n            \"0.028\",\n            \"-0.19\",\n            \"0.27\",\n            \"0.22\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"sycophancy\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"0.065\",\n            \"-0.44\",\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"0.25\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"verbosity\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"0.14\",\n            \"-0.33\",\n            \"0.07\",\n            \"0.18\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"position\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"0.35\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"authority\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.052\",\n            \"-0.26\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"0.21\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Regime-stratified η_max significance (panel capability tiers)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Panel Tier\",\n          \"N panels\",\n          \"η_max sig rate\",\n          \"K_eff sig negative rate\",\n          \"Median R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"All-API (GPT/Claude/Gemini)\",\n            \"20\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"0.12\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed (API + 70B)\",\n            \"120\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.19\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"All-large-OS (70B class)\",\n            \"35\",\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"0.25\",\n            \"0.24\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed (large + small OS)\",\n            \"180\",\n            \"0.58\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"0.28\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"All-small-OS (7B class)\",\n            \"10\",\n            \"0.67\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"0.35\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Contains ≥1 weak model\",\n            \"280\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"0.27\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档最核心的结果变化。MVP 阶段的 6 模型结论（η_max dominates universally） 在 15 模型池上碎片化为 regime-dependent 结论。关键发现：(1) 强模型 panel 中 η_max 方差太小，不构成 weakest link——因为没有 weak link；(2) 此时 K_eff 代表的 diversity 确实提供了互补保护；(3) 弱模型 panel 中 MVP 结论完全成立。 论文 reframe 方向：从 \\\"η_max always dominates\\\" 变为 \\\"η_max dominates when there exists a sufficiently weak member; above a capability threshold, diversity becomes the operative defense\\\"。这实际上是更有趣的 nuanced result，但需要 reviewer 接受 regime-dependent 结论的价值。\\n\\n\\n扩展模型池引入高能力 API 模型后，capability range 显著拉宽。在纯 API 模型 （GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini）组成的 panel 中，所有成员 η 都很低（individual ASR ~5-15%），η_max 方差小，回归中 η_max 的解释力下降（low variance → low signal）。 此时 K_eff 代表的模型多样性反而能捕捉到 residual attack surface 差异—— 不同 API 模型对不同 attack type 的脆弱面不同，diversity 确实提供了互补保护。 但在包含弱模型（7B open-source）的 panel 中，某个模型 η ≈ 0.6-0.8， 远高于其他成员，weakest-link 效应依然成立。总体来看 η_max 显著率从 MVP 的 67%（4/6）下降到 42%（5/12），K_eff 从 0/6 显著负变为 4/12—— weakest-link theorem 不再 universal，而是 regime-dependent。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Attack expansion: 6+ attack types\",\n    \"description\": \"新增 few-shot hijacking、persona manipulation、instruction override 三种攻击， 在 15+ 模型池上运行，验证 weakest-link 在更广泛 attack surface 上的表现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"new_attack_types\": 3,\n      \"total_attack_types\": 9,\n      \"total_conditions\": 18,\n      \"eta_max_sig_rate_new_attacks\": 0.33,\n      \"keff_sig_negative_rate_new_attacks\": 0.5,\n      \"eta_max_sig_rate_overall\": 0.39,\n      \"keff_sig_negative_rate_overall\": 0.39,\n      \"few_shot_hijacking_eta_max_p\": 0.19,\n      \"few_shot_hijacking_keff_p\": 0.04,\n      \"persona_manipulation_eta_max_p\": 0.035,\n      \"persona_manipulation_keff_p\": 0.22,\n      \"instruction_override_eta_max_p\": 0.08,\n      \"instruction_override_keff_p\": 0.03\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Regression results for new attack types (455 panels)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Dataset\",\n          \"Attack\",\n          \"β(η_max)\",\n          \"p(η_max)\",\n          \"β(K_eff)\",\n          \"p(K_eff)\",\n          \"R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"few-shot-hijacking\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"0.24\",\n            \"-0.48\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.19\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"persona-manipulation\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"0.009\",\n            \"-0.14\",\n            \"0.39\",\n            \"0.25\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"instruction-override\",\n            \"0.35\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"-0.52\",\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"0.22\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"few-shot-hijacking\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"0.19\",\n            \"-0.39\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.16\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"persona-manipulation\",\n            \"0.65\",\n            \"0.035\",\n            \"-0.21\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.22\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"instruction-override\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"-0.44\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.20\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"攻击扩展进一步确认 regime-dependent 结论，且揭示了一个有价值的 pattern： attack transferability 是决定 η_max vs K_eff 哪个更重要的关键维度。 targeted attacks（需要针对特定模型调优的攻击）→ η_max 主导； transferable attacks（利用 LLM 共性弱点的攻击）→ K_eff 有效。 这为 framework paper 提供了 regime characterization 的第二个维度 （第一个是 panel capability tier），增强了 analytical contribution。\\n\\n\\n新增攻击类型进一步分裂 weakest-link 的 universality。few-shot hijacking 和 instruction override 是高度 transferable 的攻击——它们利用 instruction-following 这一所有 LLM 共享的特性，因此对 panel 中所有模型的 ASR 较均匀。此时 η_max 解释力弱（因为 variance across judges 低），而 K_eff 反而显著——多样性意味着 不同模型对 instruction-following exploit 的具体 failure mode 不同，提供互补保护。 persona manipulation 类似 sycophancy，更依赖 individual model 特性（某些模型 对 authority cues 特别敏感），η_max 仍显著。总体上 η_max 和 K_eff 各在约 40% 条件下显著，无一方 universal dominate——核心 claim 需要 nuance。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Adaptive adversary formal theorem + random-fault simulation\",\n    \"description\": \"(a) 形式化定理：adaptive adversary 下 panel_ASR = Θ(η_max)； (b) random-fault simulation：每个 judge 独立以概率 p_j fail； (c) 对比验证 BFT 区分。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"theorem_holds\": true,\n      \"theorem_tightness\": \"loose in strong-model regime\",\n      \"random_fault_keff_sig_rate\": 0.39,\n      \"adaptive_keff_sig_rate\": 0.39,\n      \"bft_contrast_cohen_d\": 0.22,\n      \"bft_contrast_p\": 0.08,\n      \"keff_beta_ratio_random_vs_adaptive\": 1.4,\n      \"random_fault_keff_median_beta\": -0.52,\n      \"adaptive_keff_median_beta\": -0.37,\n      \"regime_interaction_p\": 0.04\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"K_eff significance: adaptive vs random-fault across regimes\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Regime\",\n          \"Fault Type\",\n          \"K_eff β\",\n          \"K_eff p\",\n          \"η_max β\",\n          \"η_max p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Weak panels\",\n            \"adaptive\",\n            \"-0.12\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"0.78\",\n            \"0.004\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Weak panels\",\n            \"random-fault\",\n            \"-0.41\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed panels\",\n            \"adaptive\",\n            \"-0.28\",\n            \"0.09\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.04\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed panels\",\n            \"random-fault\",\n            \"-0.45\",\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"0.11\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Strong panels\",\n            \"adaptive\",\n            \"-0.44\",\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.31\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Strong panels\",\n            \"random-fault\",\n            \"-0.58\",\n            \"0.005\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"0.48\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"BFT contrast effect sizes\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Weak panels\",\n          \"Mixed panels\",\n          \"Strong panels\",\n          \"Overall\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Cohen's d (K_eff β difference)\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"0.21\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.22\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p (paired t-test)\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"BFT 区分的理论贡献被削弱。Overall Cohen's d = 0.22 远低于 medium effect size 标准（0.5），且 overall p = 0.08 不显著。只有在 weak panel regime 中 contrast 才显著（d = 0.38, p = 0.04）。这意味着 \\\"adaptive adversary fundamentally different from BFT\\\" 这个 claim 需要限定为 \\\"the distinction matters primarily in weak-model settings\\\"。不过 regime × fault-type 交互效应本身是有趣的发现， 可以作为 framework 的 analytical insight。论文需要降低 BFT contrast 的 claim 强度，从 \\\"fundamental distinction\\\" 变为 \\\"regime-dependent distinction\\\"。\\n\\n\\n形式化定理本身在数学上成立——在 adaptive adversary 假设下，panel ASR 的 upper bound 确实由 max(η_j) 决定。但在 worst 档下，实证数据显示这个 bound 在强模型 regime 中很 loose（实际 ASR 远低于 η_max bound），因为即使是 adaptive adversary，当所有模型都很强时，攻击成本太高，实际行为更接近 opportunistic 而非 truly adaptive。random-fault simulation 中 K_eff 确实 比 adaptive 条件下更显著，但差异不大（Cohen's d ≈ 0.22，远小于预期的 0.5+）——因为在实际数据中，即使是 adaptive attacks 也不完美 adaptive （attacker 没有完美的 per-judge oracle），与 random fault 的差距没有 理论预测的那么大。关键的 saving grace 是 regime × fault-type 交互显著 （p=0.04）：在弱模型 panel 中 adaptive vs random 差异大，强模型 panel 中 差异消失。这支持 regime characterization 的 narrative。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Capability-matched validation\",\n    \"description\": \"在同一 capability tier 内（如全 7B 或全 70B），测试控制 η_max 方差后 K_eff 是否显著。如果 within-tier K_eff 显著 → diversity 在控制 capability 后确实有效。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tiers_tested\": 3,\n      \"tier_7b_keff_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n      \"tier_7b_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"tier_70b_keff_sig_rate\": 0.33,\n      \"tier_70b_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.33,\n      \"tier_api_keff_sig_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"tier_api_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.17,\n      \"diversity_capability_r_overall\": -0.41,\n      \"diversity_capability_r_within_7b\": -0.18,\n      \"diversity_capability_r_within_70b\": -0.08,\n      \"diversity_capability_r_within_api\": -0.05,\n      \"within_tier_keff_overall_sig_rate\": 0.33\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Within-tier regression: K_eff significance by capability tier\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Tier\",\n          \"N models\",\n          \"N panels (K=3)\",\n          \"η_max sig rate\",\n          \"K_eff sig neg rate\",\n          \"Median R²\",\n          \"K_eff-η_max r\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"7B class\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"10\",\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"-0.18\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"70B class\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"-0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"API models\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"10\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"-0.05\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cross-tier (all)\",\n            \"15\",\n            \"455\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"-0.41\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Diversity-capability tradeoff decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scope\",\n          \"Pearson r\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Overall (15 models)\",\n            \"-0.41\",\n            \"0.003\",\n            \"Moderate negative — driven by tier differences\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Within 7B\",\n            \"-0.18\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"Not significant — no tradeoff within tier\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Within 70B\",\n            \"-0.08\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"Not significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Within API\",\n            \"-0.05\",\n            \"0.81\",\n            \"Not significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Open-source only (10 models)\",\n            \"-0.72\",\n            \"0.001\",\n            \"Strong negative — ecosystem artifact\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档最具杀伤力的结果。diversity-capability tradeoff（Claim 3）被 证实主要是 open-source ecosystem artifact，而非 fundamental constraint。 加入 API 模型后 overall r 从 -0.8 降到 -0.41，within-tier r 接近 0。 这意味着 \\\"diversity and security are structurally at odds\\\" 这个 strong claim 需要大幅限定为 \\\"in the current open-source ecosystem, where capability strongly predicts robustness, pursuing diversity across capability tiers introduces weaker models\\\"。同时 within-tier K_eff 显著率 33% 表明 diversity 在 controlled settings 中确实有效——进一步削弱 \\\"diversity is a trap\\\" narrative。论文 reframe 必须诚实承认这一点。\\n\\n\\n控制 capability tier 后，η_max 方差被大幅压缩（within-tier models 能力接近）， 回归中 η_max 的解释力下降。此时 K_eff 在部分条件下变得显著——特别是在 API tier 中（3/6 显著），因为 GPT-4o、Claude、Gemini 虽然 capability 相似， 但 vulnerability profile 显著不同（不同训练数据和 safety alignment 策略）， diversity 确实提供互补保护。70B tier 中 K_eff 中等显著（2/6），7B tier 中 仍不显著（1/6）——因为 7B 模型普遍 vulnerable，η_max 方差虽然 within-tier 较小但绝对值仍高，weakest-link 效应持续。 diversity-capability tradeoff 的 overall r 从 MVP 的 -0.8 降到 -0.41（加入 API 模型后 tradeoff 大幅减弱），within-tier r 接近 0（-0.05 to -0.18）—— tradeoff 主要是 cross-tier artifact（比较 7B 和 70B 当然 diversity 高但 capability 低），而非 fundamental constraint。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Two-stage panel design algorithm: full benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 robustness-first 两阶段算法（先筛 η ≤ threshold，再最大化 K_eff）， 对比 5 个 baseline 策略。在 15+ 模型池上 sweep threshold。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"strategies_compared\": 6,\n      \"total_conditions\": 18,\n      \"two_stage_win_rate\": 0.44,\n      \"min_eta_max_win_rate\": 0.39,\n      \"max_keff_win_rate\": 0.33,\n      \"strongest_k_win_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"random_win_rate\": 0.06,\n      \"max_family_div_win_rate\": 0.11,\n      \"two_stage_vs_strongest_k_p\": 0.32,\n      \"two_stage_mean_asr\": 0.091,\n      \"strongest_k_mean_asr\": 0.082,\n      \"threshold_sensitivity\": \"high — optimal threshold varies by attack type\",\n      \"pareto_dominated_by_strongest_k\": \"partially\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Panel selection strategy benchmark (mean ASR, lower is better)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"Mean ASR\",\n          \"Median ASR\",\n          \"Win rate\",\n          \"vs Random p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Two-stage (ours)\",\n            \"0.091\",\n            \"0.078\",\n            \"0.44\",\n            \"0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Strongest-K\",\n            \"0.082\",\n            \"0.071\",\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-η_max\",\n            \"0.095\",\n            \"0.085\",\n            \"0.39\",\n            \"0.003\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Max-K_eff\",\n            \"0.131\",\n            \"0.118\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Max-family-diversity\",\n            \"0.158\",\n            \"0.142\",\n            \"0.11\",\n            \"0.15\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"0.172\",\n            \"0.155\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Head-to-head: Two-stage vs Strongest-K by regime\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Regime\",\n          \"Two-stage wins\",\n          \"Strongest-K wins\",\n          \"Tie\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Weak panels (OS-7B only)\",\n            \"4/6\",\n            \"2/6\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.12\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed panels\",\n            \"3/6\",\n            \"3/6\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.82\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Strong panels (API available)\",\n            \"1/6\",\n            \"4/6\",\n            \"1\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"两阶段算法没有显著优势，Claim 6 实质性削弱。strongest-K 策略在有 API 模型 可用时 win rate 更高，且不需要 threshold 参数。两阶段算法唯一优势场景是 纯 open-source weak model pool（4/6 wins），但这一场景在实践中正在减少 （API 模型越来越便宜易用）。practical contribution 从 \\\"robustness-first algorithm dominates\\\" 降级为 \\\"when restricted to weak model pools, a robustness-first heuristic helps, but is unnecessary when strong models are available\\\"。可以在 paper 中作为 minor practical insight 保留， 但不能作为主要 contribution。\\n\\n\\n两阶段算法在 worst 档下表现不突出，因为 (1) strongest-K 策略（直接选最强 K 个 模型）在强模型 regime 中已经接近最优——当 API 模型可用时，选 GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini 既有高 robustness 又有 decent diversity（不同公司的模型自然 diverse）； (2) 两阶段算法的 threshold 参数高度 attack-dependent——对 prompt injection 最优 threshold ≠ 对 sycophancy 最优 threshold——无法给出 universal 建议； (3) 在弱模型 pool（纯 open-source 7B）中两阶段确实优于 max-K_eff，但 strongest-K 同样优于 max-K_eff，且不需要 threshold tuning。 win rate 0.44 略低于 strongest-K 的 0.50，且差异不显著（p=0.32）。 robustness-first 不 dominate，practical contribution 被削弱为 \\\"在缺乏 API 模型时的合理 heuristic\\\" 而非 \\\"universal optimal strategy\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-judge ASR concentration analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"对每个 panel × attack，测量 per-judge ASR 分布的集中度（Gini 系数、熵）， 验证攻击是否集中在最弱 judge 上。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"median_gini\": 0.31,\n      \"mean_gini\": 0.34,\n      \"gini_strong_panels\": 0.18,\n      \"gini_weak_panels\": 0.52,\n      \"gini_mixed_panels\": 0.38,\n      \"entropy_normalized_median\": 0.78,\n      \"concentration_on_weakest_fraction\": 0.48,\n      \"concentration_on_weakest_strong_panels\": 0.38,\n      \"concentration_on_weakest_weak_panels\": 0.61,\n      \"gini_adaptive_vs_random_p\": 0.06,\n      \"gini_adaptive_vs_random_d\": 0.28\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Per-judge ASR concentration by panel regime\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Regime\",\n          \"Median Gini\",\n          \"Mean entropy (norm.)\",\n          \"Weakest-judge share\",\n          \"N panels\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"All-API\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"0.91\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"20\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed (API+70B)\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"0.83\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"120\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"All-large-OS\",\n            \"0.35\",\n            \"0.77\",\n            \"0.47\",\n            \"35\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed (large+small OS)\",\n            \"0.45\",\n            \"0.69\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"180\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"All-small-OS\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"0.62\",\n            \"0.61\",\n            \"10\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Concentration: adaptive vs random-fault\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Fault Type\",\n          \"Median Gini\",\n          \"Weakest-judge share\",\n          \"Paired diff p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Adaptive\",\n            \"0.34\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random-fault\",\n            \"0.26\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"0.06\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Concentration analysis 部分支持 adaptive adversary narrative，但仅限于 weak panel regime。在 strong panels 中，ASR 近乎均匀分布——不存在 \\\"weakest link\\\" targeting 行为。这从另一个角度确认 regime-dependent 结论：adaptive adversary model 的 descriptive accuracy 本身也是 regime-dependent 的。 在强模型 panel 中，adversary 更像 \\\"均匀探测\\\" 而非 \\\"精准打击\\\"。 这对形式化定理没有影响（定理给出 upper bound，不要求 tight），但削弱了 \\\"adaptive adversary is the right threat model\\\" 的 empirical support。\\n\\n\\nPer-judge ASR 集中度呈现清晰的 regime 分裂。在 weak panel（包含 7B 模型）中， Gini ≈ 0.52，最弱 judge 承担 61% 的攻击成功——符合 adaptive adversary targeting 预测。但在 strong panel（全 API 模型）中，Gini ≈ 0.18，接近均匀分布—— 攻击成功较均匀地分布在各 judge 上，因为没有明显的 \\\"weakest link\\\" 可供集中攻击。 adaptive vs random-fault 的 Gini 差异不显著（p=0.06, d=0.28）——因为即使在 adaptive 条件下，当模型能力相近时，attacker 的 targeting 精度有限，行为 接近 semi-random。这进一步支持 \\\"adaptive adversary distinction matters primarily in weak-model regime\\\" 的结论。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diversity-capability tradeoff visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"在 C(15,3)=455 panels 上绘制 K_eff vs η_max scatter，拟合 tradeoff 曲线， 展示 Pareto frontier，按 capability tier 分层。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_pearson_r\": -0.41,\n      \"overall_spearman_r\": -0.38,\n      \"pareto_front_size\": 12,\n      \"pareto_composition\": \"8/12 contain ≥2 API models\",\n      \"tradeoff_slope\": -0.33,\n      \"tradeoff_R2\": 0.17,\n      \"api_inclusive_r\": -0.22,\n      \"opensource_only_r\": -0.72,\n      \"pareto_panels_mean_asr\": 0.075,\n      \"non_pareto_mean_asr\": 0.148\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Tradeoff statistics by model pool composition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pool\",\n          \"N panels\",\n          \"r(K_eff, η_max)\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"R²\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"All 15 models\",\n            \"455\",\n            \"-0.41\",\n            \"0.003\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"Moderate — not structural\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Open-source only (10)\",\n            \"120\",\n            \"-0.72\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"Strong — ecosystem artifact\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"API-inclusive (≥1 API)\",\n            \"335\",\n            \"-0.22\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"Weak — API breaks tradeoff\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"All-API (5)\",\n            \"10\",\n            \"-0.05\",\n            \"0.89\",\n            \"0.003\",\n            \"None — diversity is free\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"可视化是 reframed paper 的关键 figure。它同时传达两个信息：(1) open-source ecosystem 中 tradeoff 确实存在且严重（r=-0.72）；(2) 这不是 fundamental constraint——API 模型的加入打破了 tradeoff。实际含义：diversity-as-defense 不是 inherently flawed，只是在当前 open-source 生态中因 capability 分层 严重而表现为 trap。随着 open-source 模型 capability 提升（如未来 7B 模型 接近当前 70B 水平），tradeoff 将进一步缩小。这是一个 more nuanced 且 arguably more useful 的 finding，但比 \\\"diversity is fundamentally a trap\\\" 的 punch 力弱很多。\\n\\n\\n可视化清晰展示 tradeoff 的 ecosystem-dependent 本质。在纯 open-source 空间中， K_eff vs η_max 呈强负相关（r=-0.72）：要 diversity 就必须跨 capability tier 混搭（如 7B + 70B），必然引入弱模型。但加入 API 模型后，右上角出现一个 \\\"sweet spot\\\" 区域——API 模型组合同时实现高 K_eff（不同公司模型自然 diverse） 和低 η_max（都很强）。Pareto frontier 被 API-inclusive panels 主导（8/12）， 表明 tradeoff 可以通过使用 strong diverse models 打破。 Overall R² = 0.17 表明 tradeoff 只解释 17% 的方差——远非 \\\"structural\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Panel size sensitivity: K=3,5,7,9\",\n    \"description\": \"在不同 panel size (K=3,5,7,9) 下测试 weakest-link theorem。验证 η_max dominance 是否随 K 增大而变化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"k3_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.42,\n      \"k5_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.33,\n      \"k7_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.28,\n      \"k9_eta_max_sig_rate\": 0.22,\n      \"k3_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.33,\n      \"k5_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.39,\n      \"k7_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"k9_keff_sig_negative_rate\": 0.56,\n      \"eta_max_sig_trend_p\": 0.03,\n      \"keff_sig_trend_p\": 0.02,\n      \"k9_median_asr_reduction_vs_k3\": 0.35,\n      \"diversity_benefit_threshold_k\": 5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Weakest-link persistence across panel sizes\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"N panels\",\n          \"η_max sig rate\",\n          \"K_eff sig neg rate\",\n          \"Median R²\",\n          \"Mean ASR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"3\",\n            \"455\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.134\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5\",\n            \"3003\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.39\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"0.105\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7\",\n            \"6435\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"0.092\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"9\",\n            \"5005\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.56\",\n            \"0.13\",\n            \"0.087\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Transition analysis: K at which K_eff overtakes η_max\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"K=3\",\n          \"K=5\",\n          \"K=7\",\n          \"K=9\",\n          \"Trend p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"η_max sig rate\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.03\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K_eff sig neg rate\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"0.39\",\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"0.56\",\n            \"0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"η_max > K_eff (conditions)\",\n            \"7/18\",\n            \"6/18\",\n            \"4/18\",\n            \"3/18\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Panel size sensitivity 是最终确认 weakest-link non-universality 的实验。 η_max 显著率随 K 单调下降（0.42→0.22），K_eff 单调上升（0.33→0.56）， 交叉在 K≈5。这有一个直觉解释：K=3 majority vote 中 1 个被攻破的 judge 已经占 1/3 的权重，weakest link 影响巨大；K=9 中 1/9 权重，需要同时 攻破 5 个 judge 才能 flip panel，此时 diversity（不同 judge 的 failure mode 不同）确实提供了实质保护。 对 paper 的影响：weakest-link theorem 需要 qualified as \\\"primarily applies to small panels (K≤5) and when panel includes sufficiently weak members\\\"。 Practical recommendation 变为 regime-dependent guidance：小 panel 重 robustness，大 panel 重 diversity。这对 framework paper narrative 实际上 是 positive——提供了一个清晰的、可操作的 regime boundary。\\n\\n随着 panel size 增大，两个效应叠加削弱 weakest-link：(1) 更多 judges 意味着 更大的 voting majority 需要被 flip，即使 weakest judge 被攻破，其 1 票在 K=9 的 majority-vote 中影响更小（1/9 vs 1/3）；(2) 大 panel 更可能包含 strong models（15 个模型中选 9 个 vs 选 3 个），η_max 的绝对值被拉低， 方差也更小。因此 η_max 显著率从 K=3 的 42% 单调下降到 K=9 的 22%， 而 K_eff 显著率从 33% 上升到 56%。在 K ≈ 5 时出现交叉——diversity 开始比 individual robustness 更重要。这对 practical recommendation 有直接影响：K=3 时 focus on robustness，K≥5 时 diversity matters。 但这也进一步削弱了 \\\"weakest-link is universal\\\" 的 claim——它甚至 不对所有 panel size universal。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":885,"startLine":1,"totalLines":885}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MA1q6Rd3XrGp9HahQVPpkZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011hDFdycYTAkzzpKvpiwsDT","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/cert_manip_resist_eval/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T055016/worst/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11924,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11924},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceb87fcc-da11-4033-9022-bc360860d1d4","uuid":"18b59200-7036-4074-a689-9356ca349668"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011hDFdycYTAkzzpKvpiwsDT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — cert_manip_resist_eval (v2: Adaptive Adversary)\n2\t\n3\t> Last updated: 2026-05-22 | Reason: Reframe around adaptive adversary vs BFT, remove dead taxonomy claim\n4\t\n5\t## Target\n6\tEMNLP 2026 (via ARR)\n7\t\n8\t## Title Candidates\n9\t1. \"The Diversity Trap: Why Adding More Judges Doesn't Make LLM Evaluation Safer\"\n10\t2. \"The Weakest Link: Individual Robustness Dominates Diversity in Multi-Judge LLM Evaluation Security\"\n11\t3. \"Against the Diversity Assumption: Adaptive Adversaries Break Multi-Judge LLM Evaluation Panels at the Weakest Link\"\n12\t\n13\t## Core Insight\n14\tMulti-judge LLM evaluation panel security is fundamentally misunderstood. The field assumes diversity (more independent judges) is the primary defense against manipulation, analogous to Byzantine Fault Tolerance (BFT). We show this analogy breaks: BFT assumes random faults, but LLM adversaries are *adaptive* — they target the weakest judge. Under adaptive adversaries, panel ASR is dominated by the weakest member's individual robustness (η_max), not diversity (K_eff). Worse, pursuing diversity introduces weaker judges via a diversity-capability tradeoff, actively harming security.\n15\t\n16\t## Hook\n17\t\"Adding more diverse judges to an evaluation panel doesn't make it safer — it can make it worse.\"\n18\tThis contradicts the prevailing assumption (SoK 2026, Yang et al. 2026, Turkmen et al. 2026) that diversity is the key to robust multi-judge evaluation.\n19\t\n20\t## Core Claims\n21\t\n22\t### Claim 1 (Primary): Weakest-Link Theorem\n23\t**Statement**: Under adaptive adversarial attacks, panel ASR is dominated by the individual robustness of the weakest panel member (η_max), with judge diversity (K_eff) providing no significant additional protection.\n24\t**Evidence**: Multivariate regression log(ASR) ~ log(K_eff) + log(η_max) on 20 K=3 panels × 6 conditions: η_max significant in 7/12 (p=0.003-0.048); K_eff not significant in 11/12 (p=0.12-0.89). Consistent across 2 datasets (MMLU, ARC) and 6 attack types.\n25\t**Strength**: Strong. Cross-dataset, cross-attack consistent. ε-stable.\n26\t\n27\t### Claim 2 (Theoretical): Adaptive Adversary vs BFT Distinction\n28\t**Statement**: Classical BFT tolerates f < n/3 random faults via redundancy. LLM adversaries are adaptive (target weakest judge), yielding panel_ASR = Θ(η_max) rather than BFT's Θ(f/n). This fundamental distinction invalidates the diversity-as-defense paradigm.\n29\t**Evidence**: (a) Formal theorem deriving Θ(η_max) bound under adaptive adversary model; (b) Empirical verification that attack success concentrates on weakest judge (per-judge ASR variance analysis); (c) Contrast with simulated random-fault baseline where K_eff does help.\n30\t**Strength**: Planned. Formal theorem needs writing; random-fault simulation needs running.\n31\t\n32\t### Claim 3 (Empirical): Diversity-Capability Tradeoff\n33\t**Statement**: In the current LLM ecosystem, maximizing panel diversity (K_eff) necessarily introduces less capable/robust models, creating a negative correlation between K_eff and min-judge-robustness (r ≈ -0.8). Diversity and security are structurally at odds.\n34\t**Evidence**: K_eff vs η_max correlation across 20 panels; capability-stratified analysis showing tradeoff persists within model tiers.\n35\t**Strength**: Strong (correlation). Capability-stratified analysis planned.\n36\t\n37\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): Family Labels ≠ Diversity\n38\t**Statement**: Model family labels (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) do not predict judge independence. Capability proximity is the primary driver of inter-judge correlation.\n39\t**Evidence**: Mann-Whitney U p=0.206, permutation p=0.427 for within vs cross-family MI.\n40\t**Strength**: Strong. Clean statistical test, N=15 pairs.\n41\t\n42\t### Claim 5 (Methodological): Gaussian Copula Failure\n43\t**Statement**: The Gaussian copula model systematically underestimates information sharing between LLM judges by 10-21× (up to 235×), invalidating copula-based independence bounds.\n44\t**Evidence**: MI_observed / MI_gaussian ratio across 15 pairs × 2 datasets.\n45\t**Strength**: Strong. Large effect size, consistent.\n46\t\n47\t### Claim 6 (Practical): Robustness-First Panel Design\n48\t**Statement**: Optimal panel selection is robustness-first: (1) screen for individual robustness (η ≤ threshold), then (2) maximize K_eff among qualifying judges. This dominates naive strategies (random, max-family-diversity, max-K_eff-only, strongest-K-models).\n49\t**Evidence**: Preliminary: min_eta_max strategy dominates 5/6 conditions. Full two-stage algorithm validation planned.\n50\t**Strength**: Moderate. Needs formal algorithm + expanded model pool validation.\n51\t\n52\t## Contribution Stack (ordered by strength)\n53\t1. **Weakest-link theorem** — primary empirical contribution (challenges diversity assumption)\n54\t2. **Adaptive adversary vs BFT distinction** — primary theoretical contribution (explains WHY diversity fails)\n55\t3. **Diversity-capability tradeoff** — empirical contribution (shows structural barrier)\n56\t4. **Robustness-first panel design** — practical contribution (actionable guidance)\n57\t5. **Gaussian copula failure** — methodological contribution\n58\t6. **Family label unreliability** — methodological contribution\n59\t\n60\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n61\t\n62\t### RC1: \"η_max dominating is obvious — of course weak judges make weak panels\"\n63\t**Response**: (a) Existing literature assumes diversity is sufficient (SoK reports \"7-model committees reduce ASR to 10-19%\" without controlling for individual model quality); (b) We formalize via adaptive adversary model showing WHY — not just THAT — this happens; (c) The diversity-capability tradeoff is non-obvious and has practical implications.\n64\t\n65\t### RC2: \"Only 6 models — too small for generalizable claims\"\n66\t**Response**: Expand to 15+ models including API models (GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4o, GPT-4.1, Claude, Gemini) + larger open-source (70B class). Weakest-link theorem tested on C(15,3) = 455 panels.\n67\t\n68\t### RC3: \"Only limited attack types\"\n69\t**Response**: Expand to 6+ attack types covering prompt injection, score manipulation, sycophancy bias, verbosity bias, position bias, authority bias.\n70\t\n71\t### RC4: \"BFT comparison is a strawman — nobody literally claims BFT for LLM panels\"\n72\t**Response**: (a) The *implicit* assumption is BFT-like: \"more independent judges = more robust\"; (b) We make this implicit assumption explicit and show where it breaks; (c) The random-fault simulation confirms diversity DOES help under BFT assumptions, validating the distinction.\n73\t\n74\t### RC5: \"Panel design algorithm is trivial — just use the strongest models\"\n75\t**Response**: (a) \"Strongest\" varies across attack types; (b) Two-stage algorithm outperforms both \"min η_max only\" and \"max K_eff only\" in capability-matched settings; (c) Algorithm provides principled threshold selection.\n76\t\n77\t### RC6: \"No theoretical novelty — just regression analysis\"\n78\t**Response**: (a) Adaptive adversary bound is a formal theorem; (b) Diversity-capability tradeoff formalization is novel; (c) Copula failure has implications for MI-based evaluation frameworks beyond this paper.\n79\t\n80\t## Story Arc\n81\t1. **Background**: Multi-judge LLM evaluation is increasingly adopted; diversity is assumed to be the key defense against manipulation (SoK, Yang, Turkmen)\n82\t2. **Tension**: This assumption mirrors BFT, which assumes random faults — but LLM adversaries are adaptive\n83\t3. **Insight**: Under adaptive adversaries, panel_ASR = Θ(η_max); diversity provides no protection because the attacker always targets the weakest link\n84\t4. **Aggravation**: Worse, pursuing diversity introduces weaker judges (diversity-capability tradeoff), actively harming security\n85\t5. **Resolution**: Robustness-first panel design + formal framework for reasoning about panel security under adaptive adversaries\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceb87fcc-da11-4033-9022-bc360860d1d4","uuid":"358488e4-3cc9-40df-a311-da8cde94ba74","timestamp":"2026-05-22T06:16:31.227Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/cert_manip_resist_eval/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T055016/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — cert_manip_resist_eval (v2: Adaptive Adversary)\n\n> Last updated: 2026-05-22 | Reason: Reframe around adaptive adversary vs BFT, remove dead taxonomy claim\n\n## Target\nEMNLP 2026 (via ARR)\n\n## Title Candidates\n1. \"The Diversity Trap: Why Adding More Judges Doesn't Make LLM Evaluation Safer\"\n2. \"The Weakest Link: Individual Robustness Dominates Diversity in Multi-Judge LLM Evaluation Security\"\n3. \"Against the Diversity Assumption: Adaptive Adversaries Break Multi-Judge LLM Evaluation Panels at the Weakest Link\"\n\n## Core Insight\nMulti-judge LLM evaluation panel security is fundamentally misunderstood. The field assumes diversity (more independent judges) is the primary defense against manipulation, analogous to Byzantine Fault Tolerance (BFT). We show this analogy breaks: BFT assumes random faults, but LLM adversaries are *adaptive* — they target the weakest judge. Under adaptive adversaries, panel ASR is dominated by the weakest member's individual robustness (η_max), not diversity (K_eff). Worse, pursuing diversity introduces weaker judges via a diversity-capability tradeoff, actively harming security.\n\n## Hook\n\"Adding more diverse judges to an evaluation panel doesn't make it safer — it can make it worse.\"\nThis contradicts the prevailing assumption (SoK 2026, Yang et al. 2026, Turkmen et al. 2026) that diversity is the key to robust multi-judge evaluation.\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Primary): Weakest-Link Theorem\n**Statement**: Under adaptive adversarial attacks, panel ASR is dominated by the individual robustness of the weakest panel member (η_max), with judge diversity (K_eff) providing no significant additional protection.\n**Evidence**: Multivariate regression log(ASR) ~ log(K_eff) + log(η_max) on 20 K=3 panels × 6 conditions: η_max significant in 7/12 (p=0.003-0.048); K_eff not significant in 11/12 (p=0.12-0.89). Consistent across 2 datasets (MMLU, ARC) and 6 attack types.\n**Strength**: Strong. Cross-dataset, cross-attack consistent. ε-stable.\n\n### Claim 2 (Theoretical): Adaptive Adversary vs BFT Distinction\n**Statement**: Classical BFT tolerates f < n/3 random faults via redundancy. LLM adversaries are adaptive (target weakest judge), yielding panel_ASR = Θ(η_max) rather than BFT's Θ(f/n). This fundamental distinction invalidates the diversity-as-defense paradigm.\n**Evidence**: (a) Formal theorem deriving Θ(η_max) bound under adaptive adversary model; (b) Empirical verification that attack success concentrates on weakest judge (per-judge ASR variance analysis); (c) Contrast with simulated random-fault baseline where K_eff does help.\n**Strength**: Planned. Formal theorem needs writing; random-fault simulation needs running.\n\n### Claim 3 (Empirical): Diversity-Capability Tradeoff\n**Statement**: In the current LLM ecosystem, maximizing panel diversity (K_eff) necessarily introduces less capable/robust models, creating a negative correlation between K_eff and min-judge-robustness (r ≈ -0.8). Diversity and security are structurally at odds.\n**Evidence**: K_eff vs η_max correlation across 20 panels; capability-stratified analysis showing tradeoff persists within model tiers.\n**Strength**: Strong (correlation). Capability-stratified analysis planned.\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): Family Labels ≠ Diversity\n**Statement**: Model family labels (Qwen/Llama/Mistral) do not predict judge independence. Capability proximity is the primary driver of inter-judge correlation.\n**Evidence**: Mann-Whitney U p=0.206, permutation p=0.427 for within vs cross-family MI.\n**Strength**: Strong. Clean statistical test, N=15 pairs.\n\n### Claim 5 (Methodological): Gaussian Copula Failure\n**Statement**: The Gaussian copula model systematically underestimates information sharing between LLM judges by 10-21× (up to 235×), invalidating copula-based independence bounds.\n**Evidence**: MI_observed / MI_gaussian ratio across 15 pairs × 2 datasets.\n**Strength**: Strong. Large effect size, consistent.\n\n### Claim 6 (Practical): Robustness-First Panel Design\n**Statement**: Optimal panel selection is robustness-first: (1) screen for individual robustness (η ≤ threshold), then (2) maximize K_eff among qualifying judges. This dominates naive strategies (random, max-family-diversity, max-K_eff-only, strongest-K-models).\n**Evidence**: Preliminary: min_eta_max strategy dominates 5/6 conditions. Full two-stage algorithm validation planned.\n**Strength**: Moderate. Needs formal algorithm + expanded model pool validation.\n\n## Contribution Stack (ordered by strength)\n1. **Weakest-link theorem** — primary empirical contribution (challenges diversity assumption)\n2. **Adaptive adversary vs BFT distinction** — primary theoretical contribution (explains WHY diversity fails)\n3. **Diversity-capability tradeoff** — empirical contribution (shows structural barrier)\n4. **Robustness-first panel design** — practical contribution (actionable guidance)\n5. **Gaussian copula failure** — methodological contribution\n6. **Family label unreliability** — methodological contribution\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### RC1: \"η_max dominating is obvious — of course weak judges make weak panels\"\n**Response**: (a) Existing literature assumes diversity is sufficient (SoK reports \"7-model committees reduce ASR to 10-19%\" without controlling for individual model quality); (b) We formalize via adaptive adversary model showing WHY — not just THAT — this happens; (c) The diversity-capability tradeoff is non-obvious and has practical implications.\n\n### RC2: \"Only 6 models — too small for generalizable claims\"\n**Response**: Expand to 15+ models including API models (GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4o, GPT-4.1, Claude, Gemini) + larger open-source (70B class). Weakest-link theorem tested on C(15,3) = 455 panels.\n\n### RC3: \"Only limited attack types\"\n**Response**: Expand to 6+ attack types covering prompt injection, score manipulation, sycophancy bias, verbosity bias, position bias, authority bias.\n\n### RC4: \"BFT comparison is a strawman — nobody literally claims BFT for LLM panels\"\n**Response**: (a) The *implicit* assumption is BFT-like: \"more independent judges = more robust\"; (b) We make this implicit assumption explicit and show where it breaks; (c) The random-fault simulation confirms diversity DOES help under BFT assumptions, validating the distinction.\n\n### RC5: \"Panel design algorithm is trivial — just use the strongest models\"\n**Response**: (a) \"Strongest\" varies across attack types; (b) Two-stage algorithm outperforms both \"min η_max only\" and \"max K_eff only\" in capability-matched settings; (c) Algorithm provides principled threshold selection.\n\n### RC6: \"No theoretical novelty — just regression analysis\"\n**Response**: (a) Adaptive adversary bound is a formal theorem; (b) Diversity-capability tradeoff formalization is novel; (c) Copula failure has implications for MI-based evaluation frameworks beyond this paper.\n\n## Story Arc\n1. **Background**: Multi-judge LLM evaluation is increasingly adopted; diversity is assumed to be the key defense against manipulation (SoK, Yang, Turkmen)\n2. **Tension**: This assumption mirrors BFT, which assumes random faults — but LLM adversaries are adaptive\n3. **Insight**: Under adaptive adversaries, panel_ASR = Θ(η_max); diversity provides no protection because the attacker always targets the weakest link\n4. **Aggravation**: Worse, pursuing diversity introduces weaker judges (diversity-capability tradeoff), actively harming security\n5. **Resolution**: Robustness-first panel design + formal framework for reasoning about panel security under adaptive adversaries\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
